     ddiisskkiinnffoo — get information about disk device

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ddiisskkiinnffoo [--cciittSSvvww] _d_i_s_k _._._.
     ddiisskkiinnffoo [--ll] --pp _d_i_s_k _._._.
     ddiisskkiinnffoo [--ll] --ss _d_i_s_k _._._.

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ddiisskkiinnffoo utility prints out information about a disk device, and op‐
     tionally runs a naive performance test on the device.

     The following options are available:

     --vv  Print fields one per line with a descriptive comment.

     --cc  Perform a simple measurement of the I/O read command overhead.

     --ii  Perform a simple IOPS benchmark.

     --ll  In case of --pp or --ss modes prepend each line of an output with a de‐
         vice name using a tab character as a separator.

     --pp  Return the physical path of the disk.  This is a string that identi‐
         fies the physical path to the disk in the storage enclosure.

     --ss  Return the disk ident, usually the serial number.

     --SS  Perform synchronous random write test (ZFS SLOG test), measuring time
         required to write data blocks of different size and flush disk cache.
         Blocks of more then 128KB are written with multiple parallel opera‐
         tions.

     --tt  Perform a simple and rather naive benchmark of the disks seek and
         transfer performance.

     --ww  Allow disruptive write tests.

     If given no arguments, the output will be a single line per specified de‐
     vice with the following fields: device name, sectorsize, media size in
     bytes, media size in sectors, stripe size, stripe offset, firmware cylin‐
     ders, firmware heads, and firmware sectors.  The last three fields are
     only present if the information is available.

